// aug15b aieka reactive divergence_000000 (2026-08-16). INTERP-side.
//
// `&x` mints its OWN cell and mirrors x into it with a CROSS-CYCLE
// `set_var`, so reading through the reference reported x's PREVIOUS
// value on every cycle x changed. Here the struct field came out
// `{c: 0}` on the cycle in0 became 1, the connect sampled that, and
// v4 never moved off 0.
//
// The write path never had the problem: `ConnectDeref` resolves the
// reference through `Env::byref_chain` to the referent and writes
// THERE. Reading just never did the same lookup — one side of the
// chain was followed and the other wasn't, and that asymmetry was the
// whole bug. `Deref` now resolves the same way (registering its wake
// interest on the resolved id too), so `*r` and `x` agree within a
// cycle, as `(x, *r)` in 01 shows directly.
// schedule-v1: cap=80 events=640; in0=i64:1
{let v1 = (&in0, i64:1 / in0); let v3 = {c: *v1.0}; let v4 = i64:0; let v6: i64 = v3.c; v4 <- in0 ~ v4 + v6; v4}
